[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw (0,0)--(2,3.2);
\draw (2,3.2)--(4,0);
\draw (4,0)--(2,1.2);
\draw (2,1.2)--(0,0);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$A$};
\node[above] at (2,3.2) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (4,0) {$C$};
\node[below] at (2,1.2) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
At which vertex of this quadrilateral is the interior angle reflex?

foundation.solution_text:
The outline turns back on itself at only one vertex, and the interior angle there opens upwards, past a straight angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw (0,0)--(2,3.2);
\draw (2,3.2)--(4,0);
\draw (4,0)--(2,1.2);
\draw (2,1.2)--(0,0);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$A$};
\node[above] at (2,3.2) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (4,0) {$C$};
\node[below] at (2,1.2) {$D$};
\draw (2.429,0.943) arc[start angle=-30.964,end angle=210.964,radius=0.5];
\node at (2,2.15) {$>180^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The interior angle at $D$ is reflex.

